  "optionAName": "Credit Card",
  "optionBName": "Debit Card",
  "introText": "For everyday purchases, a credit card is the better pick if you pay the full statement balance every month, and a debit card is the better pick if you tend to carry a balance. At ModernWallet, we publish free money calculators and plain-language guides, and we compared these two cards on the points that change your bill and your risk. The credit card vs debit card choice comes down to whose money leaves first, the lender's or yours.\n\nThat difference shows up in three places. It decides what happens to your cash when a card is stolen. It also decides whether your spending builds a credit history and what you pay if a bill goes unpaid.",
